        "anchor_id": "",
        "heading": "Building a Deck in New York: Contractors, Costs, Permits and Deck Kit Options",
        "intro": "<p>Planning a deck in New York usually begins with a few big questions: Should you hire a deck builder, purchase the materials yourself or use a professionally engineered system that arrives prepared for assembly?</p><p>This guide explains the main options, what affects the cost, how permits work, what to ask a contractor and how to choose between pressure-treated wood and composite decking.</p><p>A-DIY offers a third way to complete the project: a professionally engineered deck system delivered with coordinated components prepared for assembly. You can build it yourself or hire a local handyman, carpenter or contractor to help.</p>",
        "primary_label": "Explore Deck Options",
        "primary_link": "shopify://collections/deck-kits",
        "secondary_label": "See How A-DIY Works",
        "secondary_link": "#how-it-works",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/state-seo-new-york-hero.png",
        "image_alt": "A-DIY pressure-treated wood deck with outdoor lounge seating and a fire pit in a New York backyard",
        "image_position": "50% 65%",
        "article_schema": true,
        "region_name": "New York, United States"
      }
    },
    "three_ways": {
      "type": "state-seo-three-ways",
      "blocks": {
        "way_1": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "compass",
            "title": "Hire a Deck Contractor",
            "text": "A deck builder can manage design, materials, permits, foundations, construction, inspections and cleanup. This is often the best choice when the project is highly customized or the homeowner wants one company to manage the entire job.",
            "featured": false,
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "way_2": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "tools",
            "title": "Build From Raw Materials",
            "text": "The homeowner or builder purchases lumber, hardware and decking separately, then handles the design, measurements, cuts, structural layout and assembly. This approach offers flexibility but requires more planning and construction knowledge.",
            "featured": false,
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "way_3": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "hammer",
            "title": "Use a Professionally Engineered Deck System",
            "text": "A ready-to-assemble system uses a standardized design and coordinated components prepared for assembly. A-DIY is designed for homeowners who want a real structural deck without beginning with a loose pile of raw materials or completing every cut at the property.",
            "featured": true,
            "button_label": "See Deck Kit Options",
            "button_link": "shopify://collections/deck-kits"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
