      "settings": {
        "anchor_id": "permits",
        "heading": "New York Deck Permits",
        "lead": "A permit may be required depending on the deck’s dimensions, height, location, attachment method and local rules.",
        "body": "<p>The New York State Uniform Code establishes minimum construction standards throughout the state except New York City. Local cities, towns, villages and counties generally administer and enforce the applicable codes. New York City maintains its own construction-code and permit system.</p>",
        "callout": "Requirements may differ between neighboring municipalities.",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/state-seo-permits-diagram.png",
        "image_alt": "Exploded engineering diagram of an A-DIY deck kit showing decking, joists, beams and footings",
        "card_heading": "Questions to Ask the Building Department",
        "city_heading": "New York City",
        "city_text": "<p>New York City homeowners must follow current Department of Buildings requirements. The city may require approved plans and design work completed by a New York State licensed professional engineer or registered architect.</p>"
      }
    },
    "diagrams": {
      "type": "state-seo-diagrams",
      "settings": {
        "anchor_id": "diagrams",
        "heading": "What Do A-DIY Engineering Diagrams Show?",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/state-seo-engineering-diagrams.png",
        "image_alt": "Pressure-treated A-DIY deck sections stacked before assembly",
        "list": "<p><strong>Diagrams for an applicable A-DIY configuration may show:</strong></p><ul><li>Overall dimensions and structural layout</li><li>Beam and joist locations</li><li>Post locations</li><li>Lumber dimensions and type</li><li>Major connections</li><li>Assembly configuration</li></ul>",
        "text": "<p>The building department may still request property specific information, such as a survey, site plan, setbacks, foundation details, stairs, railings, attachment details or professionally stamped documents.</p><p>Requirements vary by municipality, and the local building department has final authority. A-DIY diagrams can support a permit application but do not guarantee approval.</p>"
      }
    },
